RING    Use provided access token directly (bypasses\n                               stored refresh tokens; token expires in ~1h)\n                               ($GOG_ACCESS_TOKEN)\n      --enable-commands=\"\"     Comma-separated list of enabled commands;\n                               dot paths allowed (restricts CLI)\n      --disable-commands=\"\"    Comma-separated list of disabled commands;\n                               dot paths allowed\n      --gmail-no-send          Block Gmail send operations (agent safety)\n  -j, --json                   Output JSON to stdout (best for scripting)\n  -p, --plain                  Output stable, parseable text to stdout (TSV;\n                               no colors)\n      --results-only           In JSON mode, emit only the primary result (drops\n                               envelope fields like nextPageToken)\n      --select=STRING          In JSON mode, select comma-separated fields\n                               (best-effort; supports dot paths). Desire path:\n                               use --fields for most commands.\n  -n, --dry-run                Do not make changes; print intended actions and\n                               exit successfully\n  -y, --force                  Skip confirmations for destructive commands\n      --no-input               Never prompt; fail instead (useful for CI)\n  -v, --verbose                Enable verbose logging\n      --version                Print version and exit\n\nCommands:\n  ls [flags]\n    List files in a folder (default: root)\n\n  search <query> ... [flags]\n    Full-text search across Drive\n\n  get <fileId>\n    Get file metadata\n\n  download <fileId> [flags]\n    Download a file (exports Google Docs formats)\n\n  copy <fileId> <name> [flags]\n    Copy a file\n\n  upload <localPath> [flags]\n    Upload a file\n\n  mkdir <name> [flags]\n    Create a folder\n\n  delete (rm,del) <fileId> [flags]\n    Move a file to trash (use --permanent to delete forever)\n\n  move <fileId> [flags]\n    Move a file to a different folder\n\n  rename <fileId> <newName>\n    Rename a file or folder\n\n  share <fileId> [flags]\n    Share a file or folder\n\n  unshare <fileId> <permissionId>\n    Remove a permission from a file\n\n  permissions <fileId> [flags]\n    List permissions on a file\n\n  url <fileId> ...\n    Print web URLs for files\n\n  comments <command>\n    Manage comments on files\n\n  drives [flags]\n    List shared drives (Team Drives)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":66,"aggregated":"Usage: gog drive (drv) <command> [flags]\nBuild: v0.13.0 (5cd913e)\n\nGoogle Drive\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                   Show context-sensitive help.\n      --color=\"auto\"           Color output: auto|always|never\n  -a, --account=STRING         Account email for API commands\n                               (gmail/calendar/chat/classroom/drive/docs/slides/contacts/tasks/people/sheets/forms/appscript/ads)\n      --client=\"\"              OAuth client name (selects stored credentials +\n                               token bucket)\n      --access-token=STRING    Use provided access token directly (bypasses\n                               stored refresh tokens; token expires in ~1h)\n                               ($GOG_ACCESS_TOKEN)\n      --enable-commands=\"\"     Comma-separated list of enabled commands;\n                               dot paths allowed (restricts CLI)\n      --disable-commands=\"\"    Comma-separated list of disabled commands;\n                               dot paths allowed\n      --gmail-no-send          Block Gmail send operations (agent safety)\n  -j, --json                   Output JSON to stdout (best for scripting)\n  -p, --plain                  Output stable, parseable text to stdout (TSV;\n                               no colors)\n      --results-only           In JSON mode, emit only the primary result (drops\n                               envelope fields like nextPageToken)\n      --select=STRING          In JSON mode, select comma-separated fields\n                               (best-effort; supports dot paths). Desire path:\n                               use --fields for most commands.\n  -n, --dry-run                Do not make changes; print intended actions and\n                               exit successfully\n  -y, --force                  Skip confirmations for destructive commands\n      --no-input               Never prompt; fail instead (useful for CI)\n  -v, --verbose                Enable verbose logging\n      --version                Print version and exit\n\nCommands:\n  ls [flags]\n    List files in a folder (default: root)\n\n  search <query> ... [flags]\n    Full-text search across Drive\n\n  get <fileId>\n    Get file metadata\n\n  download <fileId> [flags]\n    Download a file (exports Google Docs formats)\n\n  copy <fileId> <name> [flags]\n    Copy a file\n\n  upload <localPath> [flags]\n    Upload a file\n\n  mkdir <name> [flags]\n    Create a folder\n\n  delete (rm,del) <fileId> [flags]\n    Move a file to trash (use --permanent to delete forever)\n\n  move <fileId> [flags]\n    Move a file to a different folder\n\n  rename <fileId> <newName>\n    Rename a file or folder\n\n  share <fileId> [flags]\n    Share a file or folder\n\n  unshare <fileId> <permissionId>\n    Remove a permission from a file\n\n  permissions <fileId> [flags]\n    List permissions on a file\n\n  url <fileId> ...\n    Print web URLs for files\n\n  comments <command>\n    Manage comments on files\n\n  drives [flags]\n    List shared drives (Team Drives)","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-publisher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780494041412}}
